-74973/selection/ca860b265d5df30ff377b3d4906b0379041b93ff357a88ae2699ab4322582300" "q-74973/selection/76133ffb7a972126cdddaa83fd607090b1cc937c8886d0b6913aca50b865ee0b" "q-74973/selection/93284caab3b6b29210848e33495447bea1eb6b8cbdeaa83e7b487846b3459647"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74973" :question/id #uuid "87a94cdf-c793-5534-931c-84a973feddef" :question/math-academy-id "q-74973" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74973/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f892805c-2c2c-5105-91ba-353aefe7b7f2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74973"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110754/selection/e6a7043e863a085f9dae1f84128328c6663027614997fba954494180a9a2fae8" :answer/id #uuid "896928e3-84d1-5e3a-8a5b-a7bd0278686e" :answer/type :answe