S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74972/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f892805c-2c2c-5105-91ba-353aefe7b7f2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74972"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34456/selection/46be21da955020d839354414e4bab32becedc183edbb97b687bbb332f7b34c2c" :answer/id #uuid "cd5fe755-84a3-511b-a9b0-ba292895d1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34456/selection/b2e4e54fd1ffe14672806546f84d375c871564a93e8f3efef1c69bc800ed4854" :answer/id #uuid "16527d5b-70ee-570f-a60a-3dcf48bbf88a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34456/selection/8d680fde32d9fe125ce8983a8a262ba522b4be4377bdcabbab688b5527f6b7a4" :answer/id #uuid "ac57c1f9-fafb-55ee-a274-595deddb1f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{alig