lon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74981/selection/a4f8fa3fc4437e2f60949d22fe4eb7887148246c20bf257341818087f48a02e1" :answer/id #uuid "0b66a55d-97fc-56b3-9fe6-cb519b1b4429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74981/selection/1df0225bac81a15029dcff9d08f0816a8c60e53a5cc91c9a52866598d7448e39" :answer/id #uuid "68623634-3a2f-5cc9-88ff-f5418cd6f11f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74981/selection/692830286adf26521000408fe712351f731595ed20cbba49c833a8272584b75e" :answer/id #uuid "98fad079-d0c6-536f-9d4c-a22d176357ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74981/selection/7d7155360af92913a343ba10a7f19af21239bc11bd424bb959a260939fa917a6" :answer/id #uuid "c2c19441-8ec8-