lready in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74981/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection/5e94c403f9e9babdebf5c6146cea7f93e3cb862b47f4de1c0dc512c18e2fdde1" :answer/id #uuid "eca0194e-300f-5258-bf49-19ea7c725c2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection/065b541a46d3148ef64574dc2a0f74915c9dc3ba4fbc74e7210274c80451bbf9" :answer/id #uuid "ac42e78f-64bb-585c-b7c9-e3c655a04a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection/773803521a970b4e75dfc1981b1da4d60749629b98e2b5192772539a49ca6ccc" :answer/id #uuid "3fd310b0-2fc2-522b-b3b9-32ac49b4a2a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection/730a56fbd16668b2dcb25683404d08d8842c660f2c715db8da9312eeb8c301fc" :answer/id #uuid "28c8de76-f1e1-5814-8845-f5ba1ad4cfac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection/9c00d6fd68c1443e90ca7de5605f95a92efad5ebad510128d00432cb7cc426e6" :answer/id #uuid "3595d1da-bc78-5c85-8d01-bae36894af9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "396363a6-ab56-57a5-b948-c3590c2ac1a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74979/selection/065b541a46d3148ef64574dc2a0f74915c9dc3ba4fbc74e7210274c80451bbf9" :answer-field/choices ["q-74979/selection/5e94c403f9e9babdebf5c6146cea7f93e3cb862b47f4de1c0dc512c18e2fdde1" "q-74979/selection/065b541a46d3148ef64574dc2a0f74915c9dc3ba4fbc74e7210274c80451bbf9" "q-74979/selection/773803521a970b4e75dfc1981b1da4d60749629b98e2b5192772539a49ca6ccc" "q-74979/selection/730a56fbd16668b2dcb25683404d08d8842c660f2c715db8da9312eeb8c301fc" "q-74979/selection/9c00d6fd68c1443e90ca7de5605f95a92efad5ebad510128d00432cb7cc426e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74979" :question/id #uuid "9a90968f-6d5f-5ad5-b488-01f80de8a4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74979" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74979/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74979"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110853/selection/6dcdacfe6250159f1c19254ba9ed8d031f6f9f7fab290de1175e198c6e82f4ac" :answer/id #uuid "cea3a04d-8bf2-59d3-830e-cfe3f74d3c37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110853/selection/f7f5a4d1db6df83cb70912461500bb689772c5f13d0f84b73d8d7a93d8911767" :answer/id #uuid "3e08923d-bcef-58d2-aa69-b274835ac8d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110853/selection/d46a8d6d68e7723d23e41d87f88e5874a9f3f8cfad4c440bda265a9ac1b0043f" :answer/id #uuid "1457ea26-7280-5675-88c8-99a63f49b6a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110853/selection/c395e3ae71eb36dcb736cd81a25cdfa7a6dfc2bd32b960db84c492228e8e3e51" :answer/id #uuid "1c228d93-2d2d-5bf5-81bc-2e83fde2212d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{alig