vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120326 :question/answer-fields 17592186118431] {:db/id "q-35694/selection/ma-v1/aa188f34c8ec08df72ce725c54cdd04a5ac0631c73f6e2d8edc4dc63f0910db9/e52e86de9b54eaab9f12989b9f493a161a740e8994a38bc879275a84612354cc" :answer/id #uuid "6e24140a-d221-5ea9-ad45-24ee777875d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35694/selection/ma-v1/aa188f34c8ec08df72ce725c54cdd04a5ac0631c73f6e2d8edc4dc63f0910db9/86ea1ae350e8e052cceeb2500b403af5360eea49e17a2ba0e895cb6970db47a2" :answer/id #uuid "c395728a-602c-578c-8f62-b24acf6684ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35694/selection/ma-v1/aa188f34c8ec08df72ce725c54cdd04a5ac0631c73f6e2d8edc4dc63f0910db9/bbaecc0205b46b820016b8b740d1d7cb2293bca0bed9b9a00e5c57df6b22aa49" :answer/id #uuid "b6b13ddc-037a-5c78-b23e-615cbd0340b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35694/selection/ma-v1/aa188f34c8ec08df72ce725c54cdd04a5ac0631c73f6e2d8edc4dc63f0910db9/45664166bd684573a5e11