{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35694/selection/ma-v1/aa188f34c8ec08df72ce725c54cdd04a5ac0631c73f6e2d8edc4dc63f0910db9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "94a6d1f6-41e9-5c64-a297-ba78da7a6452" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "1c27d068-7397-5355-a45a-69157718315d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "62a5eb31-85f6-5491-bdfb-22164d6d663e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" :answer/id #uuid "51295dae-777f-55a1-8529-c0bc227cbd80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "2a4efa26-98ad-5706-a25d-61600653663a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e47fee-aa38-55f7-8077-4f11336ba88b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76327/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-76327/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-76327/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-76327/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-76327/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" "q-76327/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76327" :question/id #uuid "463453a7-4d4a-51d4-b218-335de29d4bcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76327" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=-4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot (-4)=8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76327/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection/3f578909f036d5b31814071cdf2dd3754a9a8b2cc81ae785e5bdb8f88b22a803" :answer/id #uuid "e7b242f0-d224-5eba-88ba-c22ab0a2851b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "a9e896ce-0227-5f49-b81d-e4de50e47342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "9393a102-025b-55b1-842c-d8eefcd4dbb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "b10f180c-aef8-52cd-a48f-673e7ccc49c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "769d7df4-e981-5de5-a227-c808dc86c355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3487d8b6-7685-5a2b-9d22-6837b3e87883" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110972/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-110972/selection/3f578909f036d5b31814071cdf2dd3754a9a8b2cc81ae785e5bdb8f88b22a803" "q-110972/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-110972/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-110972/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-110972/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110972" :question/id #uuid "61b7884b-8bb2-5c64-8e97-dc45271c3539" :question/math-academy-id "q-110972" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=-29 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6 & -29 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-3)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-1)+(-2)+(-3)=-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110972/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110972"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9aba64fe-a0af-5801-a808-4da19bd5da59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "64aa075a-24a2-5970-9664-1d1befbbbb52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" :answer/id #uuid "2896cb60-a383-5bb9-93ff-c917bb8e016a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f579d489-c656-584a-b3c4-7dcd5d4bf8e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "61632226-f1f4-5a81-9b93-f51b47d619c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa35db90-0b21-5c1d-a7e7-d80d761721f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76322/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-76322/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-76322/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-76322/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" "q-76322/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-76322/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76322" :question/id #uuid "a474b0ef-b7c4-59e9-85d4-8b00ed5acce4" :question/math-academy-id "q-76322" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 36\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{12}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+3\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 3=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76322/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76322"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "9900986f-d09f-5168-ad40-61f805f28e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "afe3a446-5618-5621-b4f5-39feb5214d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" :answer/id #uuid "478a4df8-9d20-5824-a82c-9be96d9d7db5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a67fcef5-6a6b-5dea-a779-51db1fe83c63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4ec65416-0d63-5292-92bd-999a3814f60c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07074f8b-e3b8-5c50-8d2f-69ee4582070d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110909/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" :answer-field/choices ["q-110909/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-110909/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-110909/selection/ecb9607f5814f7e8aae688b43cb1f0b18dfc9bc3691d021eee7c54175032ff32" "q-110909/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110909/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110909" :question/id #uuid "6ee4526d-564d-5328-b11a-a4978f3ab8b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110909" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 18 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 18 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 24\\end{aligned}] &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second row of the RREF matrix above, we see that the system of equations has no solution.\n\nTherefore, ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110909/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120451 :question/answer-fields 17592186119181] {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "78473c31-5180-5e5c-925d-466b63fc73e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "218a1a93-1f3b-52b9-937c-625ff59c376a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "b34c4c16-5919-5414-8463-159401f05824" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/3f578909f036d5b31814071cdf2dd3754a9a8b2cc81ae785e5bdb8f88b22a803" :answer/id #uuid "0dccfdbe-6159-50cc-91ad-cf3d3fc25136" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4dbba0a6-46e6-5b55-8970-de419896a86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb5d2a4-f07b-549c-bd80-bc4c50f63d95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/3f578909f036d5b31814071cdf2dd3754a9a8b2cc81ae785e5bdb8f88b22a803" "q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-75588"] :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-8,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+7\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-8+0+7=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75588/selection/ma-v1/356c1a693f4d7d29934c730800b71382bd51308a65dccb6f9e8218cd7e3e9a5b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4816"] :question/problem "Consider the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/308390111ffcb243fb8612b873317302c966df288001b28c6d9b02f5946aac94.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/a7df5d5b19c15a0e5f7b9d1dc93d810ca41b70c84d28c770a0d15521b14d1374.png) Find a basis of $S=\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_2=1\\cdot \\mathbf{a}_1+1\\cdot \\mathbf{a}_3\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector $\\mathbf{a}_2$ can be removed from $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$ without changing the span. So $S = \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$ is spanned by just $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_3\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_3\\},$ that is to say,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/e13b964d4391f86125a17302c70af51040c331eb76393ebb39a1fef65dab569d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6237"] :question/problem "Consider the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/ea1fe153d54f6a769e3d13177bfede1eb467525feb255fbcfd7ec88efe58b733.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/075599a7512d1105b9c6ad3acf3f4d043cb60c2aedeb8f53532045390c29f1e9.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/73b2b16a58acd290d040047339b0db3c79de19c0af04303e010a2d16e75bb94b.png) Find a basis of $S=\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3 \\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_3 \\},$ that is to say, \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/c5383ad51988564756ba754cbd6107f487fd0b32be0013f8a89bb78a6900f540.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6257"] :question/problem "The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,$ $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ $\\mathbf{a}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{a}_4$ are given below. Determine whether $\\mathcal{B} = \\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3, \\mathbf{a}_4 \\}.$ If that is the case, find $x_1 + x_2 + x_3,$ where $\\mathbf{a}_4=x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3.$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/1d282bb39042b44ed346503f3c7c4213b02089bbc7d833e82a5d95eb49f4db28.png)" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $\\mathcal{B}$ is indeed a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3,\\mathbf{a}_4 \\}.$ So, we want to find $x_1, x_2, x_3 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ such that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/a23531cb53a9b53f47d8a7080af7de78e6d7cdd7fa3a3632c37a720c7e8ba92c.png)\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $\\mathcal{B}$ is indeed a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3,\\mathbf{a}_4 \\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that $x_1=-5,$ $x_2=0,$ and $x_3=7,$ meaning that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/assets/ca123e2e8451fab6c7b106a5d1a05d153020854c694ec41cfb5d38de2fb3ae5f.png)\n\nTherefore, $x_1 + x_2 +  x_3 = (-5) + 0 + 7 = 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
